0. Definitions.

  "Elaine" means the server in this repository, in source or object form,
and any work based on it.

  The "Plugin Interface" is the set of functions, data layouts and
declarations that Elaine exposes to programs it loads at run time, for the
purpose of being extended by them, and documents as its plugin interface.

  An "Independent Plugin" is a program, such as a Lua script, that

    a) Elaine loads at run time;
    b) interacts with Elaine only through the Plugin Interface; and
    c) is not derived from, and does not contain, any part of Elaine other
       than what the Plugin Interface itself gives to a plugin.

